---
title: "max_repay_amount (Scallop Sui Lending Protocol)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_calc_values: compute collaterals_value and weighted_debts_value
    q_calc_values --> q_check_healthy: weighted_debts_value > collaterals_value
    q_check_healthy --> q_get_debt: obligation is unhealthy
    q_check_healthy --> q_return_zero: obligation is healthy
    q_return_zero --> [*]: return 0
    q_get_debt --> q_calc_total_debts: total_debt_amount = obligation::debt(obligation, debt_type)
    q_calc_total_debts --> q_check_dust: total_debts_value = debts_value_usd(obligation, ...)
    q_check_dust --> q_return_full: total_debts_value <= $10 (dust)
    q_check_dust --> q_calc_cap: total_debts_value > $10
    q_return_full --> [*]: return total_debt_amount
    q_calc_cap --> q_return_capped: max_repay = total_debts_value_raw * debt_scale / (5 * debt_price_raw)
    q_return_capped --> [*]: return min(max_repay, total_debt_amount)

    note right of q_check_dust
        INV-001: dust threshold = $10 USD across all debt types
        INV-002: dust positions can be fully liquidated in one call
    end note

    note right of q_calc_cap
        INV-003: 20% cap applied to TOTAL debt value across all types, not just DebtType
        INV-004: prevents splitting across debt types to circumvent liquidation cap
        INV-005: max_repay = total_debts_value_raw * debt_scale / (LIQUIDATION_CAP_DIVISOR * debt_price_raw)
    end note
